course: dictionary
lesson: 9137
title: Snappy: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives snappy four meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one you need. «Moving is one of the most stressful things grown-ups do, so they can be tired and snappy.» Snappy cannot mean smart or stylish here. The clue is tired and stressful, so it means cross and short with people.
explain: Look for clue words. In «Make it snappy», the words around it tell you someone wants you to hurry. A snappy title is short, quick and lively, the kind that grabs a reader straight away. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Check your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence. If grown-ups can be cross and short when they are tired, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If your meaning sounds silly, try another one from the dictionary.
fact: Snappy is an adjective, so it describes a noun: snappy, snappier, snappiest.
fact: Snappy can mean short, quick and lively, like a snappy title or a snappy answer.
fact: A snappy person speaks in a cross, short way.
fact: Snappy (informal) means smart and stylish, like a snappy suit.
fact: «Make it snappy» means hurry up.
exercise: «Moving is one of the most stressful things grown-ups do, so they can be tired and snappy.» What does snappy mean here? | Smart and stylish in new clothes | *Cross and short with people | Full of bright light | Hurry up, quick
exercise: A teacher says, «Make it snappy, class!» What does she want? | Stop talking and sit down for a rest | *Hurry up | Dress more smartly | Write a long story
exercise: Which word means short, quick and lively, like a title that grabs the reader? | Glum | *Snappy | Ancient | Treacherous
test: «In play, a pet should catch the toy sometimes, because always losing makes animals stressed or snappy.» What does snappy mean here? | Quick and lively, like a title | Hungry | *Cross and short | Smart and stylish
test: Jo's new trainers look very smart. Dad says, «Those are snappy!» What does he mean? | Hurry up | Noisy and loud | *Smart and stylish | Cross with you
exam: When someone suddenly acts snappy, it is often because something hard is happening in their life. Which meaning of snappy fits best? | Full of bright light | *Cross and short | Hurry up | Smart and stylish
